<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmed Ali Abdullah Saleh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1972">1972</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-abdullah-saleh">Ali Abdullah Saleh</a> is the eldest son of the Yemeni president Ali Abdullah Saleh. He commanded the Republican Guard and special forces, the best-equipped units of the army, and was widely seen as his father's intended successor. After the 2011 uprising he was removed from command and in 2013 appointed ambassador to the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Units commanded by Saleh's relatives, above all the Republican Guard under his son <b>Ahmed Ali</b>, grew into the regime's strongest forces.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Republic of Yemen · Military</a></li></ul></section>
